From: WineDroid
Subject: [PATCH] server: Let the owner of a hotkey set the foreground window.

A process may only set the foreground window when its last input is newer
than the foreground thread's. A hotkey press goes to the hotkey's owner
as WM_HOTKEY instead of input, so the owner never qualified, and
explorer's Alt+` window switcher (0043) got ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED from
SetForegroundWindow. Windows gives the hotkey's owner that right; record
the hotkey as the owner's latest input.

--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -1802,6 +1802,8 @@
     list_add_tail( &hotkey->queue->msg_list[POST_MESSAGE], &msg->entry );
     set_queue_bits( hotkey->queue, QS_POSTMESSAGE|QS_ALLPOSTMESSAGE|QS_HOTKEY );
     hotkey->queue->hotkey_count++;
+    /* like on Windows, the hotkey owner may then set the foreground window */
+    if (hotkey->queue->input) hotkey->queue->input->user_time = monotonic_time;
     return 1;
 }
 
